  "body": "I'm guessing that the reason we're forbidding the `cookie` header from being set for cross-origin requests is to prevent session-pinning attacks.\n\nHowever is there a reason we're forbidding setting the `cookie` header for requests whose \"credentials mode\" is `\"omit\"` or `\"same-origin\"`.\n\nAllowing setting the cookie headers on such requests could be useful to allow a website A to make requests to websites B using A's credentials to B rather than the user's credentials to B.\n\nNote that I'm _not_ suggesting that we make `cookie` a \"simple header\". That would be bad for the same reason that making `authorization` a \"simple header\" would be bad. I.e. that it could allow distributed brute-forcing credentials.\n",
